new travel permits for Leila Maajid six  months ago the Iraqi flew to Germany she  walked for 15 days across the Balkans  now she is waiting at Tegel Airport for  her departure flight together with other  refugees she wants to go back to Iraq it  was her own choice we were not treated  well we did not have enough food nor  enough sleep a lot of refugees here had  similar experiences they tried to apply  for asylum without success most of them  thought it would be easier to start a  new life in Germany the asylum process  for Iraqis is way too slow I cannot get  my family over here and I haven't  received a permit to stay yet at the  airport hamid majid is organising the  departure of his fellow citizens today  is especially hectic half an hour before  the flight he has to make a last-minute  booking for an additional 20 refugees  since October we have over 50 refugees a  week that want to return to Iraq in  January these numbers doubled last week  we had 86 today it's going to be 92 and  this is a harsh reality for some  refugees waiting in the cold instead of  work and a new life some asylum seekers  have to wait for months before they even  registered still many don't want to give  up  actually in the flash I have been here  every day I have been waiting all day  long for my appointment but so far I  haven't been able to get in it's only a  few meters to Alejandra's Travel Agency  for weeks Iraqis have been coming to him  to book their return tickets home the  one-way flight to Iraq costs around 300  euros I always ask the clients when they  book their tickets why do you want to go  back  well we imagined a different reality  here they say we have to wait too long  for our permits and sleep in shelters  and I always say you have been through  so much already in Iraq and on the way  to Germany you could have waited to see  what Germany is really like then how do  you really see it happen come on so  cooking village dirge hunters but Leyla  Majeed doesn't want to wa